    <example xml:id="evecs-eg-rotation">
      <title>Rotation</title>
      <idx><h>Rotation</h><h>eigenvectors of</h></idx>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Let <m>T\colon\R^2\to\R^2</m> be the linear transformation that rotates counterclockwise by <m>90^\circ</m>, and let <m>A</m> be the matrix for <m>T</m>.  Find the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of <m>A</m> without doing any computations.
        </p>
      </statement>
      <solution>
        <p>
          If <m>v</m> is any nonzero vector, then <m>Av</m> is rotated by an angle of <m>90^\circ</m> from <m>v</m>.  Therefore, <m>Av</m> is not on the same line as <m>v</m>, so <m>v</m> is not an eigenvector.  And of course, the zero vector is never an eigenvector.
          </p>
<image width="60%">
<shortdescription>
<!-- FILL: Brief alt-text for this TikZ figure (linear algebra context) -->
</shortdescription>
<description>
<p>
<!-- FILL: Complete accessibility description of this TikZ figure for a linear algebra course -->
</p>
</description>
